<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liulihe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liulihe is an archaeological site in Fangshan District, south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, identified as the early capital of the Western Zhou State of Yan. Excavations since the 1970s have uncovered a walled town and a cemetery whose bronzes record the enfeoffment of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-shao">Duke of Shao</a>'s family with Yan. It is the earliest known city in the Beijing area.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liulihe.jpg" alt="Liulihe" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: N509FZ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:P70-3816977_Boxcar_at_Liulihe_(20141203133235).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
